## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to coordinate API server webhook rollout, CA rotation, and observability without service disruption. Highlights risk detection and rollback discipline.

## Key Concepts

- MutatingWebhookConfiguration
- CA bundle rotation and webhooks
- RollingUpdate strategy
- Canary deployment patterns
- cluster observability and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code using Kubernetes client (Node.js)
const k8s = require('@kubernetes/client-node');
const kc = new k8s.KubeConfig();
kc.loadFromDefault();
const k8sApi = kc.makeApiClient(k8s.AdmissionregistrationV1Api);
await k8sApi.patchMutatingWebhookConfiguration('obs-sidecar', {
  // patch body
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor TLS handshake failures and distinguish node-specific issues from cluster-wide problems?
- What are safe rollback criteria and automatic rollback triggers for webhook upgrades?

Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to perform production-grade certificate rotation with minimal risk, including detection, canary strategy, and rollback.

Key Concepts

- cert-manager rotation and Issuer/Secret management
- mTLS handshakes and trust chain validation
- canary deployments and controlled rollouts
- observability for certificate issues (logs, events, cert status)
- rollback plans and verification

Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js sketch to trigger rotation and verify (simplified)
const {execSync} = require('child_process');
try {
  // Trigger rotation by refreshing CA secret (placeholder)
  execSync('kubectl delete secret cacerts -n istio-system');
  // Wait for new certs to be issued and pods to reconcile
  console.log('Rotation initiated, awaiting reconciliation...');
} catch (e) {
  console.error(e);
}
```

Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify end-to-end trust after rotation (test client, gateway logs, and sni resolution)?
- How would you automate this process for future rotations with zero-downtime guarantees?
